{#- testing/e2e/transfer/templates/entry.yml.j2 -- the ONE entry template of the generated roster (B-r1 s8, s9 PROPOSAL;
    codex-tick417 option B; codex-tick425-426 entry identity; codex-tick430-434 R1S6-CONSTRUCTOR-CLOSURE; codex-tick435-436
    grammar_decision / separator_decision; codex-tick446 RV-5 shared grammar). Rendered per roster row by the generation
    consumer (route-r2 testing/remote_harness/tasks/generate_entries.yml, generate AND verify modes) with
    ansible.builtin.template.
    Free variables: EXACTLY lme_entry_struct, lme_entry_decl and lme_entry_context (the amended typed template-input
    contract; B r5m C1-R5M-4 + R1 s8 C1-S8-EG-INPUTS):
      lme_entry_struct  = {transfer_rel, dir, file} by B's field-role mapping entry_forms.select;
      lme_entry_decl    = the parsed checkout bytes of the admitted declaration (top key transfer), never modified;
      lme_entry_context = the construction context, bound by the loader / artifact binding BESIDE the raw declaration (not
                          inside it): refusal_grammar (the ONE admitted controller.bootstrap.refusal_grammar) and
                          path_separator (core path_admission.separator). It is the loader-side projection of the SAME
                          declarations the early verifier context projects (codex-tick446 R1S8-EARLY-CONTEXT option c);
                          R2 generate_entries.yml reconciles the two (early == loader-projected) before any render.
    Imports, both WITHOUT context, no lookup, no filesystem read:
      rf = the shared refusal macro module at the grammar's OWN declared macros_rel (C1 r4c
           testing/remote_harness/templates/macros/refusal.j2, macro G.macro = refused) -- consumed, never copied
           (codex-tick446 RV-5). TYPED OBSTRUCTION OBSTRUCTION-S9-SHARED-MACRO-REACH: the current loader proof admits a
           non-literal import only as `<ref> | relpath(<ref> | dirname)` whose target lies inside this template's
           directory (lme_manifests.py :3321-3340, :3399-3405), and a literal import only of a declared template under
           this directory (:3488-3493). Until C1-S9-SHARED-MACRO-REACH lands (codex-tick458: option i SELECTED, C1
           implements the declared-input shared-member import), the loader proof REFUSES this import (expected refusal:
           the declared-import shape message). The file the renderer actually opens is R2's join: generation renders
           with the ansible.builtin.template ACTION (generate_entries :1225; installed action/template.py :105-115, :138
           build its search path -- s10 correction: s9 cited the lookup plugin's search path, which is not this
           renderer), and the admitted member must not be shadowed by an earlier search location. Nothing here works
           around either join.
      m  = the declared pure constructor macros/entry_construct.j2.
    The output is the entry_document text byte for byte; a withheld construction writes nothing and refuses through
    `mandatory` with rf[G.macro](G, codes.render_refused, [texts.render_refused over the entry and its cause pairs as
    JSON]). `mandatory` is the ONE non-builtin filter of the closure: admitted only by the declaration-bound,
    toolchain-identity-bound C1 capability C1-S9-MANDATORY-CAPABILITY (supersedes C1-S8-EG-MANDATORY); until it lands
    the loader proof REFUSES this file. r[S.refused_key] subscripts a Jinja namespace: it is Undefined only because the
    environment's getitem falls back to attribute lookup on a non-subscriptable object (UNRUN; RV-15). -#}
{%- import lme_entry_context.refusal_grammar.macros_rel as rf without context -%}
{%- import 'macros/entry_construct.j2' as m without context -%}
{%- set tr = lme_entry_decl.transfer -%}
{%- set G = lme_entry_context.refusal_grammar -%}
{%- set S = tr.entry_forms.select -%}
{%- set r = namespace(ok=false, violations=[], entry=none, text=none) -%}
{{- m.entry_document(r, tr, G, rf, lme_entry_context.path_separator, lme_entry_struct[S.transfer_rel], lme_entry_struct[S.dir], lme_entry_struct[S.file]) -}}
{%- if r.ok -%}
{{ r.text }}
{%- else -%}
{{ r[S.refused_key] | mandatory(rf[G.macro](G, tr.entry_forms.codes.render_refused, [tr.entry_forms.texts.render_refused | format(entry=r.entry, causes=(r.violations | tojson))]) | trim) }}
{%- endif -%}
